  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PNG PSI - Papua New Guinea (01-Apr-2015-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Papua New Guinea, Malaria, Population Services International (PSI HQ)This program has the following goals: To achieve a substantial and sustained reduction in the malaria burden in PNG (reduce Annual Parasite Incidence to 41/1,000 by 2018). The objectives of this program are: Maintain high coverage of long-lasting insecticide treated bednets (LLINs) and increase the utilization of appropriate malaria prevention measures.  Maintain malaria monitoring and evaluation (M&amp;E) systems and continue to develop the national capacity for surveillance.  Maximize access to and utilization of early diagnosis and appropriate treatment for malaria (EDAT)..  Strengthen malaria advocacy, communication and social mobilization (ACSM).</narrative>
  </description>
